Date: Sun, 29 Nov 2026 02:26:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Solinear control channel

With SOLINEAR_CONTROL=1: status lines on stdout (stage, connected, error, ended), commands on stdin
(combo <name>, screen <1-12>, quit) so a launcher drives the stream without simulated key presses,
and only the address given on the command line is used (no LAN / other-network addresses).
---
 app/backend/nvcomputer.cpp       |  7 +++
 app/streaming/input/input.h      |  7 +++
 app/streaming/input/keyboard.cpp | 34 ++++++++++++++
 app/streaming/session.cpp        | 80 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 app/streaming/session.h          |  3 ++
 5 files changed, 131 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/backend/nvcomputer.cpp b/app/backend/nvcomputer.cpp
index 60f06e0..0eea85d 100644
--- a/app/backend/nvcomputer.cpp
+++ b/app/backend/nvcomputer.cpp
@@ -487,6 +487,13 @@ QVector<NvAddress> NvComputer::uniqueAddresses() const
     QReadLocker readLocker(&lock);
     QVector<NvAddress> uniqueAddressList;
 
+    // Solinear: the launcher's address is a forwarder over its own network; other addresses the host reports
+    // (LAN, another Tailscale) would skip it. Use only the address we were given.
+    if (qEnvironmentVariableIntValue("SOLINEAR_CONTROL") == 1 && !manualAddress.isNull()) {
+        uniqueAddressList.append(manualAddress);
+        return uniqueAddressList;
+    }
+
     // Start with addresses correctly ordered
     uniqueAddressList.append(activeAddress);
     uniqueAddressList.append(localAddress);
